---
import Mark from "../components/Mark.astro"
import { site, social } from "../lib/site"
import Root from "../layouts/Root.astro"

const now = new Date()
const stamp = `${now.getFullYear()}-${String(now.getMonth() + 1).padStart(2, "0")}-${String(now.getDate()).padStart(2, "0")}-${String(now.getHours()).padStart(2, "0")}${String(now.getMinutes()).padStart(2, "0")}`
const cvDownloadName = `alex-boffey-cv-${stamp}.pdf`

const channels = [
  { href: `mailto:${site.email}`, label: "Email", value: site.email },
  { href: social.linkedin, label: "LinkedIn", value: "in/alexboffey" },
  { href: social.github, label: "GitHub", value: "alexboffey" },
]
---

<Root title="About" description={site.description} quiet scene="about">
  <div class="about shell">
    <header class="about__head recede">
      <p class="about__name rise">Alex Boffey</p>
      <h1 class="about__title rise" style="--i: 1">
        Product engineer,<br />
        <span class="about__accent">with deep frontend roots</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead about__lead rise" style="--i: 2">
        Hi, I'm Alex (some people call me Boff). I'm a product engineer in
        London, nine years in, and a lifelong musician.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="about__grid">
      <section class="about__col prose reveal-children" aria-labelledby="how">
        <h2 id="how">How I work</h2>
        <p>
          I like owning a feature the whole way through: working out what the
          problem really is, then the data model, the API and the UI on top.
          Nine years of frontend means the UI is where I'm fastest, which leaves
          more time for the parts that decide whether the feature works.
        </p>
        <p>
          I keep things small so they stay easy to change. Most of the
          complexity I've had to untangle was accidental: a bad interface, or
          two things that should have stayed separate. Cutting it pays off
          twice, because a simpler system is easier to run and easier to change
          next month.
        </p>
        <p>
          The same goes for AI agents. An agent copies whatever patterns it
          finds, so a codebase with one design system, clear state patterns,
          strict types and CI checks gets consistent work out of it. That's most
          of what I mean by setting a codebase up for agents.
        </p>
        <p>
          The end-to-end tests worth having drive the whole system the way a
          user would. Happy-path assertions are easy to write and often prove
          very little. A suite can be green while the feature is broken.
        </p>

        <h2>Music &amp; audio</h2>
        <p>
          I've played guitar my whole life, mostly electric, with some classical
          on the side, and I love effects. In the band I handle the technical
          side: demos, sound design, synthesis, sampling and the live rig. When
          something needs a proper audio engineer, we get one.
        </p>
        <p>
          The live rig takes our production tracks and breaks them down into
          something the band can play against: stems, effects we can play live,
          and a cue system that runs the show. Software habits carry over. I
          don't trust a patch until I've tested it, and I keep it as simple as
          it'll go.
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside
        class="about__side reveal"
        id="contact"
        aria-labelledby="contact-h"
      >
        <a
          class="about__contact-head"
          href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
          aria-label="Email Alex"
        >
          <Mark size={28} />
          <h2 class="about__contact-title" id="contact-h">Get in touch</h2>
        </a>
        <p class="about__contact-body">
          If you're hiring, or you want to argue about design tokens, email is
          the fastest way to reach me.
        </p>

        <dl class="channels">
          {
            channels.map((channel) => (
              <div class="channel">
                <dt class="channel__label">{channel.label}</dt>
                <dd class="channel__value">
                  <a
                    href={channel.href}
                    rel={
                      channel.href.startsWith("http")
                        ? "me noopener"
                        : undefined
                    }
                  >
                    {channel.value}
                  </a>
                </dd>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>

        <div class="about__ctas">
          <a class="action action--primary" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>
            Email me
          </a>
          <a
            class="action"
            href="/alex-boffey-cv.pdf"
            download={cvDownloadName}
          >
            Download CV
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Root>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .about__head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .about__title {
    position: relative;
    font-size: var(--size-display);
    font-stretch: var(--wdth-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.96;
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .about__name {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--size-label);
    font-stretch: 88%;
    letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-label);
  }

  .about__accent {
    color: var(--incandescent);
  }

  .about__lead {
    max-width: 54ch;
  }

  .about__lead a {
    color: var(--incandescent);
  }

  .about__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .about__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 24rem);
      gap: var(--space-3xl);
      align-items: start;
    }

    .about__side {
      position: sticky;
      /* Clears the sticky nav. */
      top: calc(var(--space-lg) + 4.5rem);
    }
  }

  .about__col {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .about__side {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .about__contact-head {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    width: fit-content;
    --mark-dur: 700ms;
  }

  .about__contact-title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--size-sub);
    font-stretch: var(--wdth-title);
    color: var(--paper);
    transition: color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }

  .about__contact-head:hover .about__contact-title,
  .about__contact-head:focus-visible .about__contact-title {
    color: var(--incandescent);
  }

  .about__contact-body {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--size-small);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .channels {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .channel {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding-block: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .channel__label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--size-micro);
    font-stretch: 88%;
    letter-spacing: var(--track-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-label);
  }

  .channel__value {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--size-small);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .channel__value a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .channel__value a:hover,
  .channel__value a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--incandescent);
  }

  .about__ctas {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }
</style>
